# Diti365 — Security Agency Management System

## Read before writing any code
- `docs/prd/PRD.md` — product overview, roles, modules, architecture
- `docs/prd/01-database.md` — Phase 1 schema (SQL Server)
- `docs/prd/02-api.md` — Phase 1.5 .NET 10 API
- `docs/prd/03-web.md` — Phase 2 Next.js web
- `docs/prd/04-mobile.md` — Phase 3 React Native
- `docs/prd/05-rbac-and-nfr.md` — permissions, security, acceptance criteria
- `docs/prd/06-apk-inventory.md` — legacy feature-parity checklist

## Build order — do not skip
Database → API → Web → Mobile. Do not start a phase until the previous phase's
"Definition of Done" checklist in its doc is complete.

## Hard rules
1. Stack is fixed: SQL Server 2019+, .NET 10 Web API (controllers + MediatR + **raw ADO.NET
   calling stored procedures only — no EF Core, no Dapper, no ORM**), Next.js 15 App Router +
   TypeScript strict + Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui + TanStack Query/Table, React Native Expo SDK 51+.
2. `CompanyID` is NEVER accepted from the client. It comes from JWT claims only.
   Any request carrying companyId in route/query/body is rejected with TENANT_PARAM_FORBIDDEN.
3. Every tenant-owned table has `CompanyID` and every index leads with it.
4. Preserve legacy column names exactly (EmpID, UnitID, WcsSalaryID, BeltNo, DesignationName)
   so production data migrates 1:1. Do not "improve" naming.
5. All DB objects via ordered idempotent DbUp scripts in `db/scripts/`. No EF migrations for legacy tables.
6. No `SELECT *` in any stored procedure. Every list endpoint is paginated (default 50, max 200).
7. No business logic in controllers. No DbContext/IDbConnection in controllers.
8. HTTPS only. Never re-introduce cleartext traffic. No secrets committed.
9. Field-write endpoints accept an Idempotency-Key so the mobile offline outbox can retry safely.
10. Legacy `api/{Users|Operation|Tasks|Sales|Report}/*` routes must keep the exact envelope
    `{ Success, Status, Id, Message, Data[] }` — the shipped APK v4.8 depends on it.

## Style
- C#: file-scoped namespaces, records for DTOs, async everywhere, FluentValidation.
- TS: strict mode, no `any`, Zod schemas shared from `packages/shared`.
- Shared code (API client, Zod schemas, permission matrix, formatters) lives in `packages/shared`
  and is imported by both web and mobile. Never duplicate it.
